  "//gamma_rungs": "Rung 23 (sim_gamma, dense) RE-LANDED after the B1 varcorr sigma-hat^2 fix (2026-07-11 bug-fixes spec). Rung 24 (sim_sparse_gamma) stays BACKED OUT with a CORRECTED diagnosis: the overnight 'sparse optimizer stops short' was a misattribution -- the formula frontend's parser extracts slope REs before intercept REs, so the harness lowers (1|gp)+(1+x1..x4|ge) with ge as PRIMARY (q_p=5) and routes the DENSE kernel; it is the dense joint optimizer that lands ~2e-3 deviance above the tolPwrss=1e-13 lme4 optimum (beta[0] 2.9e-2 off, n_eval ~1018). The sparse orientation of the SAME model (gp primary, in-crate golden) lands 2e-4 above with beta 1.6e-3 and is green at its golden gates. Also: the 7.4e-3 deviance gap reported overnight compared against a default-tolPwrss lme4 value (lagged-weights artifact); the honest same-objective gap was always sub-1e-2 of that. Re-land options (user decision): fix the frontend RE ordering to formula order, route q_p>=5-with-extras to sparse, or improve the dense stage-1/2 schedule (campaign-settled -- do not reopen unilaterally). Tolerances were NOT relaxed. On re-land these are rung-18-style 2-WAY gates (no jl_formula): MixedModels' Gamma GLMM is a documented different estimator, its JSONs stay intentionally absent. See parity/README.md.",

